# =============================================================================
# Files excluded from Vercel CLI deploys (`vercel deploy`).
#
# .gitignore handles GitHub-bound exclusions; this file handles what gets
# uploaded when deploying via the CLI. The two overlap heavily but exist for
# different purposes.
# =============================================================================

# Never upload local secrets — Vercel's env var system is the source of truth.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.*.development
.env.*.preview
.env.*.production
.env.local.generated.tmp

# Build outputs and caches
.next
.vercel
node_modules
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dev tooling artifacts
.claude
coverage
.DS_Store

# Misc
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
# docs/ is design notes, seeds and runbooks — EXCEPT docs/guides, which the app READS
# AT RUNTIME (/training renders the Markdown; /api/guides/img streams the PNGs).
# Vercel applies this file to GIT deploys too ("Removed N ignored files defined in
# .vercelignore" in every build log), so a bare `docs` here deleted the guides before
# `next build` ever ran and /training rendered its error page (ENOENT) (found 2026-09-28 on the
# feat/learn-the-build preview). `docs/*` + the negation keeps everything else out.
# tests/deploy-tree.test.ts pins every runtime-read path against this file.
docs/*
!docs/guides/
